{
  "_readme": [
    "Source registry for Briefly. `scripts/seed_reference_data.py` loads this into the",
    "`sources` table; `scripts/verify_feeds.py` fetches every feed_url, honours robots.txt,",
    "and reports which ones actually work from your network.",
    "",
    "IMPORTANT — feed_verified:",
    "  false  = the URL follows the publisher's documented/published feed pattern but has NOT",
    "           been confirmed live from this machine. Run scripts/verify_feeds.py before",
    "           relying on it; correct any that have moved. Feeds get retired and moved often.",
    "  Entries with `enabled: false` need a commercial licence or an API key and are",
    "  intentionally left switched off rather than guessed at.",
    "",
    "Never add a source here that requires defeating a paywall, logging in, or ignoring",
    "robots.txt. `access: restricted` means: link out only, never store a summary.",
    "",
    "feed_category / section_feeds:",
    "  A publisher files its own stories into sections, and its section feeds say which.",
    "  `feed_category` is the section of the main feed; `section_feeds` lists further feeds,",
    "  each with the Briefly category its items are filed under. They make every section of",
    "  the app fillable from publishers' own feeds, with or without an aggregator.",
    "  Like feed_url, these follow each publisher's published feed pattern and are NOT",
    "  confirmed live from the machine that wrote this file. A feed that has moved is",
    "  reported in the run log as failed and simply contributes nothing."
  ],
